First, I isolate the absolute values: \begin{align*}
|x| &> 6\\
|x+1| &\le 7
\end{align*}Since $|x|>6,$ either $x>6$ or $x<-6.$ \begin{align*}
x+1 &\ge -7 &&\Rightarrow x \ge -8, \\
x+1 &\le 7 &&\Rightarrow x \le 6.\end{align*}When $x>6,$ combining this with the above yields $x>6.$ When $x<-6,$ combining with $x\le 6$ will always be false. Therefore, $x>6.$ \end{think} \begin{answer}All integers greater than $6$ less than or equal to $7$ have the same sum. There are a total of $\boxed{2}$ integers, $7$ and $8.$ The sum is $7+8=\boxed{15}.$ </think> <answer>15</answer>

